-- The shared vocabulary (MMS-521): one declaration for each thing two or
-- more instruments speak about, so that each can state its claim in the
-- same terms and the root (l4/lib/root.l4) can line the claims up. An
-- instrument's file imports this module and adds `<item> according to
-- <instrument>`, defined from its own rules; nothing here computes a claim.
--
-- It imports the prelude, the conventions and the takanon's introduction
-- (for the kinds of source) only, so that any module can import it — the
-- takanon's §1.1 among them, which the calculator ships.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT terms

§ `אוצר המילים המשותף — מה שכמה מסמכים מדברים עליו`

§§ `המסמך`

-- How an instrument describes itself, in its own file: which module encodes
-- it, its name, its kind as the takanon's introduction tells sources apart,
-- its date, and the two facts §29 of the Budget Foundations Law asks of what
-- it gives. A collection's root lists the instruments it includes.
@desc An instrument that may speak to a pay item.
DECLARE `instrument` HAS
    `module`        IS A STRING @desc the L4 module that encodes it
    `title`         IS A STRING @desc its name, in Hebrew
    `kind`          IS A `kind of source` @desc as the takanon's introduction tells sources apart
    `is the takanon` IS A BOOLEAN
    `issued`        IS A DATE
    `practised for all state employees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what it gives is as agreed or practised for all state employees (§29(א))
    `approved by the Finance Minister`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc what it gives was approved by the Finance Minister (§29(א))

§§ `המעסיק`

-- Who employs the teaching employee, as far as the instruments that speak
-- of the 2008 supplement tell employers apart: the State; a local
-- authority (the three large cities among them), a party to the agreement
-- of 24.1.2008; or another owner of schools (a network, a corporation), to
-- which the owners' circulars are addressed together with the local
-- authorities.
DECLARE `the teacher's employer` IS ONE OF
    `employed by the State`
    `employed by a local authority`
    `employed by another owning body`

GIVEN e IS A `the teacher's employer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an owning body` e IF
    NOT e EQUALS `employed by the State`

§§ `פריטי השכר`

-- The pay items two or more instruments speak about. Each is asked of the
-- root as one question — `the answer that governs` item case — whatever
-- instruments speak to it; a new item is a new constructor here, its
-- facts in the case below, and its claims in the instruments' files.
DECLARE `pay item` IS ONE OF
    @desc "תוספת 2008": the public-sector wage supplement of 2008 for teaching employees not in a reform
    `the 2008 public-sector supplement`
    @desc "גמול רכז פדגוגי": the pedagogical coordinator's role allowance, as a share of the combined salary
    `the pedagogical coordinator's allowance rate`
    @desc "גמול חונך": a mentor's role allowance for the interns the mentor accompanies, as a share of the combined salary
    `the mentor's allowance rate`
    @desc "גמול ניהול חטיבה צעירה": the junior-division head's role allowance, in shekels, at a full position
    `the junior-division head's allowance`

GIVEN i IS A `pay item`
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the name of the item` i IS
    CONSIDER i
    WHEN `the 2008 public-sector supplement` THEN "תוספת 2008"
    WHEN `the pedagogical coordinator's allowance rate` THEN "גמול רכז פדגוגי"
    WHEN `the mentor's allowance rate` THEN "גמול חונך"
    WHEN `the junior-division head's allowance` THEN "גמול ניהול חטיבה צעירה"

§§ `בית הספר`

-- The schools the owners' employment circulars are addressed to, one
-- circular a year for each: a recognised-unofficial special-education
-- school (תש"ף/1 … תשפ"ו/1), and a recognised-unofficial primary school of
-- the Ma'ayan HaChinuch HaTorani or Chinuch Atzmai networks (תשפ"ד/1), and
-- a recognised-unofficial special-education kindergarten (תשפ"ד/3,
-- תשפ"ה/2, תשפ"ו/2).
-- Any other school is one no owners' circular in the root speaks to.
DECLARE `the kind of school in the case` IS ONE OF
    `a recognised unofficial special-education school`
    `a Ma'ayan HaChinuch HaTorani or Chinuch Atzmai primary school`
    `a recognised unofficial special-education kindergarten`
    `another school`

§§ `המקרה`

-- What any instrument may ask about a teaching employee in a salary month,
-- in one record: an item uses the facts it needs and ignores the rest.
@desc A teaching employee's salary month, as far as any instrument speaking to a pay item asks about it.
DECLARE `teaching case` HAS
    `the salary month`                IS A DATE    @desc any day of the salary month
    `employer`                        IS A `the teacher's employer`
    `in post-primary education`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc employed in post-primary (על-יסודי) education
    `in the upper division`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc employed in the upper division (חטיבה עליונה)
    `represented by the secondary teachers' organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc represented by ארגון המורים בבתי הספר העל-יסודיים
    `in a population whose 5% step was put off` IS A BOOLEAN @desc one of the four populations the agreement of 17.6.2009 put off to October 2011
    `combined salary today`                 IS A NUMBER  @desc the combined salary at its current value, at the teacher's position
    `supplement 2001 today`                 IS A NUMBER  @desc תוספת 2001 at its current value
    `combined salary in December 2007` IS A NUMBER @desc the combined salary at its value in December 2007
    `supplement 2001 in December 2007` IS A NUMBER @desc תוספת 2001 at its value in December 2007
    `the kind of school`               IS A `the kind of school in the case` @desc the school the teacher is employed in, as the owners' circulars tell them apart
    `the interns the teacher mentors`  IS A NUMBER @desc how many interns the teacher is appointed to mentor; 0 if none
    `the classes in each grade`        IS A NUMBER @desc the classes in each grade of the division the teacher heads or coordinates

-- Whether the case's salary month is month m of year y or later: any day
-- of the month says which month it is (convention dates.start).
GIVEN c IS A `teaching case`, y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the salary month is at least` c y m IF
    (c's `the salary month`) `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- Whether the case's salary month falls in the school year that starts on
-- 1 September of year y (a yearly circular's year): from 1.9.y to 31.8.y+1.
GIVEN c IS A `teaching case`, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the salary month is in the school year from` c y IF
        `the salary month is at least` c y 9
    AND NOT `the salary month is at least` c (y PLUS 1) 9

-- Whether a yearly owners' circular reaches the case: an owner's employee,
-- in the kind of school it is addressed to, in its school year.
GIVEN c IS A `teaching case`, k IS A `the kind of school in the case`, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an owner's teacher in` c k y IF
        `is an owning body` (c's `employer`)
    AND c's `the kind of school` EQUALS k
    AND `the salary month is in the school year from` c y
